COMMAND "Ensure router marker zones" DESCRIPTION "Idempotently plant the three named scaffy:zone marker comments in api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex -- the catalog's #1 unserved accretion file (175 commits / 1283 co-change partners in 12 months per bp scaffy discover), twice ruled unservable (W1: ordering-hostile, anchors are positional text; W5: add-api-route-parity retired as scoped). This command IS the anchor repair the root-heex playbook proved: a one-time, reversible plant of a head-anchor comment at each of the router's three genuinely append-shaped AND ordering-safe neighborhoods (new pipeline definitions at the pipeline run's tail; new plugin auth-bucket wrappers ahead of the root-mounted bucket run; new workspace-scoped mirror scopes at the mirror run's tail). Each zone comment states IN WORDS the ordering contract it guards -- the same prose-pin idiom the router already uses ('mounted AFTER the :token_root block so operator statics win') -- so a future insert-at-zone is correct by construction instead of re-derived from 2400 lines. No variables: the zones are fixed artifacts, planted once, guarded by their own declaration text." LAST_UPDATED "17-07-2026-16-00-00" DOMAIN "barkpark" TAGS "scaffy", "scaffold" CONCEPT "ensure-router-zones" VARIANT "elixir" DIRECTION "add" VARIABLES

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY THIS COMMAND EXISTS — the measured append streams of router.ex
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loop-tick mining (2026-07-17): 177 commits since 2026-04 split 121 PURE_ADD
# (68%) + 22 MOSTLY_ADD (12%) vs 34 MIXED — 81% additive, the most append-
# shaped hot file in the repo. The adds decompose into FIVE streams, and the
# survey verdict differs per stream:
#
#   1. PIPELINE definitions — `pipeline :name do ... end` blocks. ~10 new
#      pipelines since April (:cycle_api, :api_grant_read #3071, :ticket_key +
#      :session_token_root (tickets), :github_webhook #1234, :public_api
#      #1171, :search_settings_admin #3168, :require_chat_access #2958,
#      :registered_chat_host, :media_processing_callback). → ZONE (op 1).
#
#   2. PLUGIN AUTH-BUCKET wrappers — `scope ... plugin_routes(scope: :x)`.
#      Five bucket adds since April (:public_api #1171, :github_webhook
#      #1234, :session_token_root + :ticket_key (tickets), the scoped :token
#      mirror #1994). Per-route plugin adds auto-fold via register_routes/1
#      (the runtime collector) and never touch this file — it is the BUCKETS
#      (new auth tiers) that accrete here. → ZONE (op 2).
#
#   3. WORKSPACE-SCOPED MIRROR scopes — `scope "/w/:workspace_slug/..."`
#      blocks mirroring a flat surface into the hard tenant boundary (scoped
#      secrets #3933/D199, scoped chat-token mint D36, scoped cycles
#      b465e591f, export/import #3012). → ZONE (op 3).
#
#   4. FLAT CORE `/v1` scopes and routes. CUT. The evidence shows flat adds
#      land NEXT TO their semantic family, not at any tail: site-deploy
#      #3223 added routes INSIDE the existing `scope "/v1/admin"` block; the
#      chat-host scopes (43c023ab0) landed flush against the `/v1/chat`
#      scope; the search-settings scopes #3168 sit directly above their
#      `[:api, :require_admin]` siblings with prose that says "the sibling
#      insights/synonyms routes stay on [:api, :require_admin] below"; the
#      restore split (2d22cbf9d) reads "mirroring the flat restore split
#      above". Contextual proximity + cross-referencing prose IS the flat
#      region's organization, and its real ordering pins are NOUN-LOCAL
#      (static /graph/orphans before dynamic /graph/:id; /access/mine before
#      /access/:id) — facts a single generic zone cannot encode. A "flat
#      scopes append here" zone would collect unrelated scopes and orphan
#      the neighbor-binding prose. This re-affirms W1's cut for the flat
#      region specifically, now with the stream isolated.
#
#   5. Routes INSIDE existing scope blocks (the site-deploy case). CUT —
#      a zone marks ONE landing site; per-scope interiors are many, and each
#      already has its owning block + local pins as the anchor.
#
# So: THREE zones, not five — planted exactly where the append stream is
# genuinely head-stable and ordering-neutral, cut with evidence where the
# file's real organization is contextual.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE ENSURE CONTRACT, ZONE SPELLING — same law as ensure-root-layout-zones
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Like every ensure-* command this guarantees an END STATE and keys each guard
# on payload text a hand edit would also produce — the zone declaration
# `scaffy:zone <name>` itself, NOT the trailing `MARK:` token. The D57
# consequences bind: a hand-planted identical zone wins (the run skips, writes
# NO receipt), and `bp scaffy remove` after such a skip exits 4 — correct,
# scaffy never owned that line. In the common case scaffy plants the zone,
# owns it, and remove retracts it byte-clean.
#
# ZONE MECHANICS — head anchor, append-below. All three ops use the proven
# idiom: anchor at a byte-unique, never-consumed block that CLOSES the
# neighborhood, plant the zone comment directly after it, and direct all
# future appends DIRECTLY BELOW the zone comment. What makes the router
# different from root.html.heex is that route ORDER is semantics here
# (Phoenix matches in declaration order), so each zone's position is chosen
# so that an append below it is ordering-safe BY CONSTRUCTION — and the
# zone comment states the contract in words, exactly like the file's
# existing prose pins. The payloads are Elixir `#` comments — stripped at
# compile, zero runtime bytes. Because the marks sit on their own comment
# lines, MIXED sweep-refactors carry or leave them whole.
#
# THE PAYOFF: a future add-plugin-bucket / add-scoped-mirror command anchors
# at these marks with plain INSERT AFTER FIRST — the mark mechanic's
# first-contact behavior done once, so every later command against this file
# starts anchored instead of surveying 2400 lines of positional text (the
# exact reason W1 and W5 had to cut it).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OP 1 — plant the pipelines zone at the tail of the contiguous pipeline run
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchor: the `:require_write` pipeline — the LAST block of the router's
# contiguous pipeline run (before the first `scope`), byte-unique (the plug
# module recurs in other pipelines, but this three-line block exists once),
# consumed by nothing. Ordering law stated in the payload: pipeline
# DEFINITIONS are position-free — each compiles to a named private plug that
# `pipe_through` references by NAME, so definition placement can never
# change route matching (the tree itself proves it: `:media_processing_
# callback` is defined ~1200 lines below its siblings, mid-scopes, and
# works). A zone here is therefore the zero-risk default landing; thematic
# adjacency to a sibling pipeline (as :api_grant_read chose, right after
# :api) stays equally legal — the zone exists so an author never has to
# prove that freedom first.
IN "api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex"
### Plant the pipelines zone after the last pipeline of the contiguous run
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: pipeline run tail :::
  pipeline :require_write do
    plug(BarkparkWeb.Plugs.RequireWritePermission)
  end
::: pipeline run tail :::
WITH
::: router-pipelines zone :::

  # scaffy:zone router-pipelines (ensure-router-zones) -- stable head anchor
  # for NEW pipeline definitions: add your `pipeline :name do ... end` block
  # DIRECTLY BELOW this comment. Pipeline definitions are POSITION-FREE --
  # each compiles to a named private plug referenced by name from
  # `pipe_through`, so a block landing here can never change route matching
  # (proof in-tree: :media_processing_callback is defined mid-scopes far
  # below and works). Ordering INSIDE a pipeline (plug order) is that
  # pipeline's own documented contract -- read its comments. Sweeps: move
  # this comment only whole, on its own lines. MARK:zone-router-pipelines
::: router-pipelines zone :::
MARK "zone-router-pipelines"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "scaffy:zone router-pipelines"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OP 2 — plant the plugin-buckets zone ahead of the root-mounted bucket run
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchor: the `:github_webhook` wrapper — the last `/v1/plugins`-mounted
# bucket before the root-mounted (`scope "/v1"`) run begins, byte-unique
# (`pipe_through(:github_webhook)` occurs once). The position IS the
# ordering contract: `/v1/plugins`-mounted wrappers are order-free among
# themselves (every plugin route path carries its own slug, so cross-bucket
# paths are disjoint), and a ROOT-mounted wrapper planted below this zone
# necessarily lands BEFORE the `:token_root` → `:session_token_root` →
# `:ticket_key` run — so it can never land after `:ticket_key`, whose
# submitter dynamic `/tickets/:id` must remain the LAST root-mounted match
# (the static-before-dynamic pin those blocks' own comments state: operator
# statics like `/tickets/inbox` must match first). An append here preserves
# that pin by construction.
IN "api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex"
### Plant the plugin-buckets zone after the github-webhook wrapper
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: github-webhook wrapper :::
  scope "/v1/plugins" do
    pipe_through(:github_webhook)

    plugin_routes(scope: :github_webhook)
  end
::: github-webhook wrapper :::
WITH
::: plugin-buckets zone :::

  # scaffy:zone plugin-buckets (ensure-router-zones) -- stable head anchor
  # for NEW plugin auth-bucket wrappers (`scope ... plugin_routes(scope:
  # :x)`; the matching `pipeline` goes in the router-pipelines zone above):
  # add the wrapper DIRECTLY BELOW this comment. Ordering contract this
  # position guards: /v1/plugins-mounted wrappers are order-free among
  # themselves (plugin paths are slug-disjoint), and a ROOT-mounted
  # (`scope "/v1"`) wrapper landing here sits BEFORE the :token_root /
  # :session_token_root / :ticket_key run below, so :ticket_key's submitter
  # dynamic `/tickets/:id` stays the LAST root-mounted match and operator
  # statics keep winning (the static-before-dynamic pin in those blocks'
  # comments). NEVER declare a bucket after :ticket_key. Per-route plugin
  # adds do NOT belong here -- they auto-fold via register_routes/1. Sweeps:
  # move this comment only whole, on its own lines. MARK:zone-plugin-buckets
::: plugin-buckets zone :::
MARK "zone-plugin-buckets"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "scaffy:zone plugin-buckets"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OP 3 — plant the scoped-mirrors zone at the tail of the /w/ mirror run
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchor: the `:scoped_media_mutate` scope — the last block of the
# workspace-scoped mirror run (before the `/api` workspace switcher),
# byte-unique (`pipe_through(:scoped_media_mutate)` occurs once). Ordering
# law stated in the payload: every scope in the mirror run owns a disjoint
# `/v1/<noun>` suffix under the shared `/w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug`
# prefix, so a NEW mirror with a NOVEL noun is order-neutral at the tail —
# nothing earlier can swallow it, and it can swallow nothing. The two ways
# an insert could break ordering are named in the zone text so they are
# refused at the point of temptation: reusing an EXISTING noun (the owning
# block's dynamics could shadow the new static — e.g. an earlier
# `/v1/media/:dataset` read would swallow `/v1/media/<literal>`; such a
# route belongs INSIDE its owning block, statics before dynamics), and a
# `/studio`-suffixed scope (the `/w/:ws/p/:proj/studio/:dataset` back-compat
# wildcard far above swallows those; they must be declared before it, with
# the scoped plugin scopes).
IN "api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex"
### Plant the scoped-mirrors zone after the scoped media mutate block
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: scoped media mutate tail :::
  scope "/w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug", BarkparkWeb do
    pipe_through(:scoped_media_mutate)

    post("/v1/media/:dataset/upload", V1.MediaController, :upload)
    patch("/v1/media/:dataset/:id", V1.MediaController, :update)
    delete("/v1/media/:dataset/:id", V1.MediaController, :delete)
  end
::: scoped media mutate tail :::
WITH
::: scoped-mirrors zone :::

  # scaffy:zone scoped-mirrors (ensure-router-zones) -- stable tail anchor
  # for NEW workspace-scoped mirror scopes: add your
  # `scope "/w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug" ...` block DIRECTLY BELOW
  # this comment. Ordering contract this position guards: every mirror above
  # owns a disjoint `/v1/<noun>` suffix, so a new mirror is order-neutral
  # here PROVIDED (a) its suffix starts `/v1/` with a NOVEL noun -- a route
  # under a noun an existing block already serves belongs INSIDE that owning
  # block, statics before dynamic `:param` segments (the /graph and
  # /access/mine idiom), because an earlier dynamic like `/v1/media/:dataset`
  # swallows a later literal -- and (b) it is NEVER a `/studio`-suffixed
  # scope: the `/w/:ws/p/:proj/studio/:dataset` back-compat wildcard far
  # above swallows those, so studio scopes are declared BEFORE that wildcard,
  # beside the scoped plugin scopes. Sweeps: move this comment only whole,
  # on its own lines. MARK:zone-scoped-mirrors
::: scoped-mirrors zone :::
MARK "zone-scoped-mirrors"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "scaffy:zone scoped-mirrors"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POSTCONDITIONS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three zone declarations present (each a verbatim substring of its op's
# payload). Holds whether this run planted them or a prior run / hand edit
# already had them — the ensure contract guarantees the END STATE. There is
# no cheap LOCAL runtime gate for the router (every mix gate compiles the
# world, A2), so the LOCAL close is grep-shaped and the compile proof is
# TIER ci: comment-only payloads in valid `#` syntax cannot change routing
# (comments are stripped before the router macros expand), and `mix compile`
# in CI reds if a plant ever landed inside a syntactic construct.
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex" CONTAINS "scaffy:zone router-pipelines"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex" CONTAINS "scaffy:zone plugin-buckets"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex" CONTAINS "scaffy:zone scoped-mirrors"
ASSERT CMD "cd api && mix compile" TIER ci
